IMPORT prelude

-- Tobacco and Vaporisers Control Act 1993 (Singapore) -- who counts as under-aged (s 2), online sales (s 2(2)), free samples
-- (s 9(2)), supply to and use by under-aged persons (ss 10, 11), minimum pack size (s 12), the prohibited-product regimes for
-- chewing tobacco, vaporisers and imitation tobacco products (ss 15, 16, 16A), Part 3A products containing a specified
-- psychoactive substance (ss 19B-19E, 19G), and the duties of responsible persons of specified premises (s 19W).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TVCA1993.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 9 of 2026 (in force 1 May 2026) shown; Parts 3A and 3B carry that annotation throughout. ss 14(8) and 16A(7) name the amending
-- Act as the Tobacco (Control of Advertisements and Sale) (Amendment) and Other Matters Act 2026; that this Act once bore the shorter
-- name is an inference.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a smoker, a vaper, a
-- retailer, a parent or a venue operator meets. Not encoded: advertising (Part 2), s 9A loyalty programmes, s 12A display ban,
-- s 13 warning notices, s 14 prescribed-substance products, s 18 licences, the evidential presumptions (ss 16B, 16C, 19M-19P),
-- drug testing (ss 19J-19L), rehabilitation (ss 19R-19U), enforcement powers and composition (Part 4). The "date prescribed"
-- that starts the under-aged phase-in, the Schedule's substances beyond their names, and the "specified premises" are fixed
-- outside the deposit and are taken as given.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Tobacco and Vaporisers Control Act 1993 -- products`

§§ `2 -- under-aged person, child, young person, online sales`

-- s 2(1) "under-aged person" means "(a) for 12 months after the date prescribed, an individual who is below 19 years of age; (b) for
-- 12 months after the end of the period in paragraph (a), an individual who is below 20 years of age; and (c) at any time after the
-- end of the period in paragraph (b), an individual who is below 21 years of age". "child" means below 16; "young person" below 21.
-- The definition says nothing about the time before the date prescribed; the encoding assumes that date has passed (inference).
GIVEN `months since the date prescribed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the under-aged age limit` MEANS
    IF `months since the date prescribed` LESS THAN 12 THEN 19
    ELSE (IF `months since the date prescribed` LESS THAN 24 THEN 20 ELSE 21)

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `months since the date prescribed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is under-aged` IF
    `age` LESS THAN `the under-aged age limit` `months since the date prescribed`

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a child` IF `age` LESS THAN 16

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a young person` IF `age` LESS THAN 21

-- s 2(2): an online sale or purchase "is regarded as a sale or a purchase in Singapore if, and only if, the purchaser is physically
-- present in Singapore and the purchased product is intended to be delivered in Singapore".
GIVEN `purchaser physically in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `delivery intended in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an online sale is a sale in Singapore` IF
    `purchaser physically in Singapore` AND `delivery intended in Singapore`

§§ `9(2) -- free samples`

-- s 9(2): a person must not distribute or give in Singapore "any free sample of a tobacco product to the public or any section of the
-- public ... other than to persons who are associated or concerned with the manufacture, distribution or sale of tobacco products".
-- (4): $10,000 or 6 months; second or subsequent conviction $20,000 or 12 months.
GIVEN `gave a free sample` IS A BOOLEAN, `recipient is in the tobacco trade` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `giving a free sample is an offence` IF
    `gave a free sample` AND (NOT `recipient is in the tobacco trade`)

§§ `10 -- supply to under-aged persons`

-- s 10(1): (a) sells, (b) buys or acquires for the purpose of giving, or (c) gives or furnishes, any tobacco product to an under-aged
-- person. Maximum fines: (d) $5,000 / $10,000; (e) $2,500 / $5,000; (f) $500 / $1,000 (second or subsequent conviction).
-- (2): a defence "if a person proves" reasonable grounds AND reasonable inquiries, or reasonable acceptance of evidence of age.
DECLARE SupplyAct IS ONE OF
    `selling`
    `buying it to give`
    `giving`

GIVEN `the act` IS A SupplyAct, `recipient is under-aged` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reasonable belief and inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved reasonable acceptance of evidence of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `supplying an under-aged person is an offence` IF
    `recipient is under-aged` AND (NOT `proved reasonable belief and inquiries`) AND (NOT `proved reasonable acceptance of evidence of age`)

GIVEN `the act` IS A SupplyAct, `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for supplying` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `selling` THEN (IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000)
    WHEN `buying it to give` THEN (IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 5000 ELSE 2500)
    WHEN `giving` THEN (IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 1000 ELSE 500)

§§ `11 -- use by under-aged persons`

-- s 11(1): an under-aged person who "(a) uses or has in the person's possession, in a public place or on a road in Singapore, any
-- tobacco product; or (b) buys in Singapore any tobacco product" -- fine not exceeding $300. (2): it does not matter whether for
-- own use or someone else's. Possession at home is not caught by (a).
GIVEN `under-aged` IS A BOOLEAN, `used or possessed in a public place or on a road` IS A BOOLEAN, `bought it in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the under-aged person commits an offence` IF
    `under-aged` AND (`used or possessed in a public place or on a road` OR `bought it in Singapore`)

`the maximum fine for an under-aged user` MEANS 300

§§ `12 -- minimum pack size`

-- s 12(1): a person must not import, distribute, sell or possess for sale any cigarette "except in the form of a package containing
-- not less than the prescribed minimum number of cigarettes" -- 20, unless the Minister gazettes another number (12(4)).
-- (2): not for import "solely for the purpose of taking them out of Singapore". (4): "cigarette" includes a cigarillo.
GIVEN `cigarettes in the package` IS A NUMBER, `gazetted minimum` IS A NUMBER, `solely for re-export` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dealing in the package is an offence` IF
    (NOT `solely for re-export`) AND `cigarettes in the package` LESS THAN `the prescribed minimum` `gazetted minimum`

-- A gazetted minimum of 0 stands for "no other number specified".
GIVEN `gazetted minimum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed minimum` MEANS
    IF `gazetted minimum` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `gazetted minimum` ELSE 20

§§ `15, 16, 16A, 19B-19D -- prohibited products`

-- s 15(1)(a)(i) chewing tobacco; s 16 "any vaporiser or any component of a vaporiser", and (7) it "is not necessary for a vaporiser
-- ... to contain tobacco or a tobacco product or tobacco substitute"; s 16A imitation tobacco products (toys or confectionery
-- resembling tobacco products). Each bans import, sale and supply, and possession, purchase and USE.
-- ss 14(3) and 15(4) exempt transit (import solely to take the thing out of Singapore). s 16 and s 16A have no such exemption.
-- s 19A: a "Part 3A product" is any tobacco product, imitation tobacco product, vaporiser or component; ss 19B-19D apply where it
-- "contains a specified psychoactive substance" (the Schedule lists etomidate, metomidate and four related compounds).
DECLARE Product IS ONE OF
    `ordinary cigarettes`
    `chewing tobacco`
    `an e-vaporiser`
    `a nicotine-free vaporiser`
    `a candy cigarette`
    `a vape pod containing etomidate`

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the product is banned outright` IF
    CONSIDER `the product`
    WHEN `ordinary cigarettes` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the product contains a specified psychoactive substance` IF
    CONSIDER `the product`
    WHEN `a vape pod containing etomidate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product, `solely for taking out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `importing is a prohibited-product offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the product`
    WHEN `ordinary cigarettes` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `chewing tobacco` THEN NOT `solely for taking out of Singapore`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ss 15(3), 16(3), 16A(3): a person must not possess (other than for supply), purchase or use the thing. 15(8), 16(6), 16A(5):
-- fine not exceeding $10,000. s 19D: possession or purchase of a Part 3A product with a specified psychoactive substance --
-- $20,000 or 10 years or both.
GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possessing it for personal use is an offence` IF
    `the product is banned outright` `the product`

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for personal possession` MEANS
    IF `the product contains a specified psychoactive substance` `the product` THEN 20000
    ELSE (IF `the product is banned outright` `the product` THEN 10000 ELSE 0)

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum years for personal possession` MEANS
    IF `the product contains a specified psychoactive substance` `the product` THEN 10 ELSE 0

-- Import. s 15(6) and 16(4): "shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 9 years" and in addition
-- liable to a fine up to $300,000. s 16A(4): fine up to $100,000 or 3 years or both; with a prior qualifying conviction $200,000
-- or 6 years. s 19B(2): "imprisonment for a term of not less than 3 years and not more than 20 years" and 5 to 15 strokes.
-- A vape pod containing etomidate is both a vaporiser (s 16) and a Part 3A product (s 19B); the heavier figure is returned.
GIVEN `the product` IS A Product, `a prior qualifying conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum years for importing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the product`
    WHEN `ordinary cigarettes` THEN 0
    WHEN `a candy cigarette` THEN (IF `a prior qualifying conviction` THEN 6 ELSE 3)
    WHEN `a vape pod containing etomidate` THEN 20
    OTHERWISE 9

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum years for importing` MEANS
    IF `the product contains a specified psychoactive substance` `the product` THEN 3 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prison is mandatory for importing` IF
    CONSIDER `the product`
    WHEN `chewing tobacco` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an e-vaporiser` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a nicotine-free vaporiser` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a vape pod containing etomidate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for importing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the product`
    WHEN `ordinary cigarettes` THEN 0
    WHEN `a candy cigarette` THEN 100000
    OTHERWISE 300000

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum strokes for importing` MEANS
    IF `the product contains a specified psychoactive substance` `the product` THEN 5 ELSE 0

-- Sale and supply. s 15(7), 16(5): mandatory imprisonment up to 6 years and a fine up to $200,000. s 19C(2): 2 to 10 years and
-- 2 to 5 strokes.
GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum years for selling` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the product`
    WHEN `ordinary cigarettes` THEN 0
    WHEN `a candy cigarette` THEN 3
    WHEN `a vape pod containing etomidate` THEN 10
    OTHERWISE 6

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum years for selling` MEANS
    IF `the product contains a specified psychoactive substance` `the product` THEN 2 ELSE 0

§§ `19E -- consumption`

-- s 19E(1): a person commits an offence "if the person smokes, inhales or otherwise consumes a specified psychoactive substance";
-- (3): it need not be consumed using a Part 3A product. s 19F: a citizen or permanent resident who consumes outside Singapore,
-- and is found to have done so by urine test under s 19J, may be dealt with as if the offence had been committed in Singapore.
GIVEN `consumed a specified psychoactive substance` IS A BOOLEAN, `consumed in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN, `found by a section 19J urine test` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consuming is an offence` IF
    `consumed a specified psychoactive substance` AND (NOT `authorised by this Act`)
        AND (`consumed in Singapore` OR (`a citizen or permanent resident` AND `found by a section 19J urine test`))

§§ `19G -- leaving products where children can reach them`

-- s 19G(1): a person "of or above 21 years of age" in possession of a Part 3A-SPS product who "knowingly or recklessly leaves" it
-- "exposed in any place" or in a container "that is not locked", and "knows that any child has, or is likely to have, access".
-- (4): not where the possession is authorised under this Act. (3): imprisonment up to 10 years; on a second or subsequent
-- conviction, 2 to 10 years.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `knowingly or recklessly left it exposed or unlocked` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew a child has or is likely to have access` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `possession authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leaving it within a child's reach is an offence` IF
    `age` AT LEAST 21 AND `knowingly or recklessly left it exposed or unlocked` AND `knew a child has or is likely to have access`
        AND (NOT `possession authorised`)

GIVEN `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum years for leaving it within reach` MEANS
    IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 2 ELSE 0

§§ `19W -- responsible persons of specified premises`

-- s 19W(1), (2): if an individual is found possessing or using a section 15 tobacco product, vaporiser or imitation tobacco product
-- on specified premises, the responsible person must tell the individual to dispose of it (and stop using it), and if the individual
-- does not, request the individual to leave. (5): failing to comply where the responsible person "knows or ought reasonably to know"
-- -- fine up to $1,000; $2,000 on a second or subsequent conviction. (6), (7): presumed to know, "until the contrary is proved", where
-- a relevant personnel knows. (9): no refund of an admission or transport fee. (10): no duty to search.
GIVEN `knew or ought reasonably to know` IS A BOOLEAN, `a relevant personnel knew` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `told the individual to dispose of it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the individual complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `asked the individual to leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the responsible person commits an offence` IF
    (`knew or ought reasonably to know` OR (`a relevant personnel knew` AND (NOT `proved the contrary`)))
        AND ((NOT `told the individual to dispose of it`) OR ((NOT `the individual complied`) AND (NOT `asked the individual to leave`)))

GIVEN `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a responsible person` MEANS
    IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the responsible person must refund the admission fee` IF FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the responsible person must search patrons` IF FALSE
